bio: |
  I am an Integrated PhD student in the Department of Physical Sciences at the **Indian Institute of Science Education and Research (IISER) Pune**, India, working under the supervision of Dr. Chandrakala Meena (IISER Pune) and Prof. Fakhteh Ghanbarnejaad (SRH University of Applied Sciences, Leipzig, Germany).

  I completed my MS (Research) at Indian Institute of Science Education and Research, Thiruvananthapuram with a CGPA of 9.23. My master's thesis was on *Stability of large dynamical systems using Gershgorin Disc Theorem* which helped me gain experience in computational skills and ability to work with large real life networks. I completed my Bachelors from Moolji Jaitha College, Jalgaon, India where I gained my experience in experimental physics as my bachelor's thesis was based on Green synthesis of nanoparticles and its application in humidity sensors.

  My research combines mathematical modeling, nonlinear dynamical systems, and computational simulations to investigate how interaction influences population and disease dynamics. I am particularly interested in how cross-scale interactions shape stability and resilience in ecological communities.
