project: |
  **PhD Project Summary:** My Integrated PhD project investigates eco-epidemiological dynamics in multi-trophic food chain systems incorporating gravity-based interaction mechanisms. I develop and analyze deterministic and network-based models in which interaction strengths between species are modulated by gravity-like kernels, capturing distance-dependent or trait-mediated coupling effects. Using stability analysis, bifurcation theory, and numerical simulations, I examine how spatially structured interactions influence disease persistence, trophic cascades, and ecosystem stability. The overall goal is to identify the conditions under which infectious processes alter food chain resilience and to derive general principles governing coupled ecological–epidemiological systems.
